# .gitattributes — line-ending policy for dotfiles-Fedora.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .editorconfig sets `end_of_line = lf`, but that only guides EDITORS — it does not
# govern what git writes on checkout/commit. This repo is cloned onto WSL from Windows
# hosts, where git can introduce CRLF. If bootstrap.sh lands on disk with CRLF its
# shebang becomes `…/env bash\r` and the interpreter dies with "bad interpreter: No such
# file or directory" — breakage that shellcheck and `bash -n` cannot see (the file is
# valid text). This makes LF a hard guarantee at the git layer.
#
# Deliberately mirrors core/.gitattributes: this repo is the template the other Linux
# OS repos are stamped from.

# Default: normalize all detected-text files to LF in the index and on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ── Executable + sourced shell — MUST stay LF or the shebang/sourcing breaks ───
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.zsh       text eol=lf

# ── Config / data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.gitconfig text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf

# /etc/wsl.conf is consumed by the Windows-side WSL service but is a Linux config
# file; LF is correct (WSL parses LF fine, and bootstrap.sh sed-templates it).
wsl/wsl.conf text eol=lf

# ── The vendored subtree — treat as generated, keep it out of diffs/reviews ────
# core/ is a byte-for-byte copy of dotfiles-core (its tree SHA is verified by
# core-integrity.sh), so it must never be normalized differently here, and marking it
# linguist-vendored keeps GitHub's language stats and PR diffs focused on the OS layer.
core/** linguist-vendored

# ── Binaries (defensive): never normalize, never diff as text ─────────────────
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.gz        binary
*.zip       binary
